  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Atelier / Maker's Mark",
    "overview": "Atelier is the default authenticated workspace: neutral surfaces, compact controls, a quiet navigation rail and fire-orange actions. The existing Maker's Mark supplies its signature. This records the implemented system alongside the supported Classic and Monolith choices; light/dark remains an independent setting.\n\nPublic sign-in is a distinct, owner-specified indigo-and-white surface with AIHR identity. Its palette is scoped locally and remains light across app themes. Its typography resolves the existing font variable. The login composition belongs to its surface brief, not to every future screen.\n\nThe native OneHR+ default has its own approved **Daily Switch** world: porcelain/graphite surfaces, a chartreuse physical attendance key and dark LCD worked-time display. It applies to schema-1 native screens, replacing their prior default city/Opal presentation. Published schema-2 compositions retain their own theme, typography, artwork and navigation; explicit cobalt/coral schema-1 accents survive. Web Atelier, public web sign-in, Performance & Talent and lifecycle styling retain their existing scope.\n\nThe native Access Pass uses the original paired Opal mountain artwork, restored by the owner specifically for sign-in. Username and password share one opaque panel and one submit action; continuation states retain existing MFA, enrollment and recovery behavior. Evidence is source inspection of `mobile/lib/{daily-switch-theme,daily-switch,daily-navigation,sign-in-background,internal-sign-in,visual,design,ui}.tsx` (the theme module is `.ts`) and tab routes. Native rendered acceptance remains pending: no iOS/Android screenshot or contrast-verification claim follows from this documentation.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat shell and cards with hairline boundaries.",
      "Compact sentence-case operational hierarchy.",
      "Orange action/focus accent in Atelier; independent indigo sign-in.",
      "Human-confirmation signature and semantic status labels.",
      "Native Daily Switch default: porcelain/graphite, chartreuse physical key, LCD and original mountain Access Pass; published tenant compositions remain authoritative."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Scoped Accent Rule",
        "body": "Use Atelier orange for actions, focus and small emphasis; keep public sign-in indigo inside its own surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "body": "Keep the shell and cards flat; use the existing small control shadow, ask-box lift and overlay shadow for their established roles.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Published Theme Rule",
        "body": "Daily Switch defaults never override a published schema-2 tenant composition.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reuse the shared card, field, button and table hooks so Atelier styling reaches new operational screens.",
      "Do keep status text alongside its color and preserve tabular figures in tables.",
      "Do preserve supported saved theme choices; Atelier supplies the fallback.",
      "Do retain visible keyboard focus and the reduced-motion path.",
      "Do use the native `mobile-*` roles only within the Daily Switch default, preserving tenant composition authority.",
      "Do keep the original mountain artwork scoped to native sign-in and announce instrument values as complete text."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't apply the public login split or indigo palette to authenticated screens by default.",
      "Don't replace the existing Atelier identity or restyle Classic and Monolith through unscoped overrides.",
      "Don't treat the presence of a dark palette as a completed contrast audit."
    ]
  }
